    "text": "By First Alert Weather ,\n1 hours ago WASHINGTON (7News) — A “supermoon” happens when a full moon coincides with the Moon’s closest approach to Earth (perigee). That slightly shorter distance makes the Moon appear a bit larger and brighter than average. For the December 2025 supermoon, the full phase peaks at 6:14 p.m.... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
